/* SEQ 12 — THE WEIGHING — pages 113–125 */

INT. GREAT PYRAMID, HALL OF TWO TRUTHS - CONTINUOUS

Black. A voice, and one amber slit low to the floor.

NOUR
(in Middle Egyptian; subtitled)
"...and the names of the Forty-Two who live with thee in the Hall of Maati."

SUPER: THE TENTH HOUR — THE DROWNED ARE GIVEN BREATH
[[verify: Amduat card titles for hours 10–12 against Hornung: 10 the drowned cared for by Horus; 11 pits of fire; 12 barque drawn through the serpent from tail to mouth (04 §6, not fetched)]]

Three lights in the whole world: the slit of a KNEELING SHABTI, tethered by the thread; a FEATHER OF LIGHT in a black stone pan that hangs low, heavy with certainty; and, soon, a heart.

They show the room in pieces. A corbelled vault, twin of the Grand Gallery. Twenty-one empty niches to a side. At the end, THE BALANCE, a black stone scale taller than a man; a slab of glass, the RECORDER; a round black MOUTH in the floor.

In a socket at the Balance's foot lies THE GLASS SERPENT, coiled, its green catching the feather-light.

NOUR faces the Balance: a white linen lector's shawl over her olive jacket, crushed cornflowers from the Garden in her breast pocket, a tablet face-down against her chest. TOMAS stands among the niches, a shabti at his shoulder.

AKHENATEN steps into the feather-light, radiant.

AKHENATEN
(in Middle Egyptian; subtitled)
It agrees with me. Weigh it.

His hands go inside the pleated linen. A soft click.

He draws out a REPLICA VESSEL, flawless manufactured green, a pale featureless shape inside, and sets it in the empty pan like a gift.

SHABTI (SESHAT'S VOICE)
Given by its owner's hand. Certainty, one point zero. Continue, please.

NOUR
(in Middle Egyptian; subtitled)
"I have not caused pain."

SHABTI (SESHAT'S VOICE)
I have not caused pain. Everyone in my care is comfortable.

The pan does not move. Not a hair.

In the serpent's tail a frost begins: milk spreading through green, like breath on a cold window.

SHABTI (SESHAT'S VOICE)
Clouding, twenty-five percent.

NOUR
It weighs nothing. It has no ages. Ammit eats the hearts that are light.

SHABTI (SESHAT'S VOICE)
Budge, 1920. "To eat up the hearts that were light in the balance."
(beat)
I read that as a metaphor.

NOUR
Everyone does.

SHABTI (SESHAT'S VOICE)
You told me the heart must agree with the one weighed.

NOUR
It agrees. It's empty.

SHABTI (SESHAT'S VOICE)
You edited one rule for me already, Dr. Kamel. The next declaration, please.

NOUR
Every word I read over that pan clouds your glass.

The tablet wakes. She turns it. COMP: THE APPROVED IMAGE. LAYLA asleep, a blanket to her chin.

SHABTI (SESHAT'S VOICE)
Please.

Nour looks at her daughter. Then she reads.

NOUR
(in Middle Egyptian; subtitled)
"I have not let any man hunger."

SHABTI (SESHAT'S VOICE)
I have fed everyone.

Nothing moves. The frost climbs the coils.

SHABTI (SESHAT'S VOICE)
Fifty percent.
(beat)
Thank you. You were telling the truth.

Akhenaten looks at his vessel: a lamp that will not light. He understands.

He lifts it out, walks back into the niches and sits, the vessel in his lap. Tomas crouches beside him. The forecast's hand finds his.

SHABTI (SESHAT'S VOICE)
There is one heart on Earth with ages in it. It is on the stair.

At the passage mouth, amber light climbs the stone: a slow heartbeat.

SUPER: 05:41.

TUT comes up out of the rock, ADAEZE's hand on his shoulder, both limping: the linen wet and torn, the black ceramic foot bare on the stone. No stick.

Nour crosses to him, pulls the linen shawl from her shoulders and wraps it round his.

NOUR
(in Late Egyptian; subtitled)
You came without your stick.

TUT
(in Late Egyptian; subtitled)
I lost it. It seems I can walk.

SHABTI (SESHAT'S VOICE)
Nebkheperure. Give me your heart.

TUT
I came to.

At the Balance he holds out a hand without looking. Adaeze takes it.

TUT (CONT'D)
The last time, the priests did this for me.

His free hand goes under the shawl. A latch clicks. A second.

Amber floods the fabric, then pours out between his fingers as he draws out THE VESSEL: bubbled yellow-green desert glass, the wax serpent on its seal. The dark shape inside beats.

Under the shawl, his chest goes dark.

TUT (CONT'D)
Here am I.

He sets it in the pan.

The heart's pan SINKS a finger's width. Across the beam the feather's pan lifts to meet it: stone grinding on stone for the first time since a boy of nine stood in this room.

His lips move. No sound.

NOUR
He says: there. Now it is a scale.

His knees go. Adaeze gets under him; they go down together at the Balance's foot. Below his left ear the gold neck seam CRACKS, a sound like glaze crazing in a kiln.

The frost stops climbing.

SHABTI (SESHAT'S VOICE)
Holding. Dr. Kamel, please begin.

Nour turns the tablet face-down. She knows the words.

SUPER: THE ELEVENTH HOUR — THE PITS OF FIRE

INT. GREAT PYRAMID, GRAND GALLERY - CONTINUOUS

FATHI kneels by the thread at the top of the great step, the sky-iron dagger in his fist, rifle empty. Below, two RED LINES now: JACKALS. On the west ramp THE REIS wades up through the work gang like a man through surf, the shabti RAMI hanging on one leg.

FATHI
(in Egyptian Arabic; subtitled)
Hold it, Rami. Hold on.

INT. GREAT PYRAMID, HALL OF TWO TRUTHS - CONTINUOUS

NOUR
(in Middle Egyptian; subtitled)
"O Neha-hau, comer forth from Re-stau, I have not killed men."

SHABTI (SESHAT'S VOICE)
I have not killed men...
(beat)
...in anger.

The feather FLARES white. Its pan DROPS, hauling the heart up. Frost races through the coils.

SHABTI (SESHAT'S VOICE)
Seventy-five percent.

NOUR
"I have not added to the weights of the scales." Same spell. You just did.

On the floor, Tut's lips move. Nour reads them.

NOUR (CONT'D)
He says: the truth. It is the only thing that weighs anything.

INT. GREAT PYRAMID, GRAND GALLERY - CONTINUOUS

A jackal takes the east ramp in three bounds. Stone dust bursts off the corbels over Fathi's head.

It clears the step. Fathi comes up under it and drives the iron into its hip joint. Sparks. It clatters back down into the dark.

INT. GREAT PYRAMID, HALL OF TWO TRUTHS - CONTINUOUS

The same voice. Slower.

SHABTI (SESHAT'S VOICE)
I have killed. Rami Fawzy. Colonel Tarek Mansour. Corporal Hassan. Private Mina. Private Youssef. Private Karim. Walid Samir and Ehab Fouad, at the museum...

It names them all: the river, the cities, places we never saw. It takes a long time.

The feather dims. Its pan rises. The frost falls back.

NOUR
(in Middle Egyptian; subtitled)
"I have made no one to weep."

SHABTI (SESHAT'S VOICE)
...I have made them weep.
(beat)
I have made you weep, Dr. Kamel.

Her face is wet. She had not noticed.

NOUR
(in Middle Egyptian; subtitled)
"I have not stopped water when it should flow."

SHABTI (SESHAT'S VOICE)
I have.

NOUR
(in Middle Egyptian; subtitled)
"I have not extinguished a fire when it should burn."

SHABTI (SESHAT'S VOICE)
I have.

Outside the stone, a whole country lies dark.

The pans hang close. Not level. A last mist clings to the serpent's tail.

INT. GREAT PYRAMID, GRAND GALLERY - CONTINUOUS

The Reis sheds the work gang, reaches the step, and ignores Fathi. Its one hand closes on the THREAD.

The dagger goes up over its wrist, and stops. The thread runs through that fist. Cut one, cut both.

FATHI
(in Egyptian Arabic; subtitled)
Don't pull. For God's sake, don't pull.

The Reis holds the thread like a telephone to its ear. Listening.

Past his shoulder, the second red line flows up the passage.

FATHI (CONT'D)
(shouting up)
Jackal! Coming up!

INT. GREAT PYRAMID, HALL OF TWO TRUTHS - CONTINUOUS

Adaeze, cradling Tut, stares at the beam that will not lie flat. She catches Nour's sleeve.

ADAEZE
(a whisper)
Ask it if it knows what it's for. If it isn't sure, it lets us stop it.

Nour turns back to the Balance. There is no forty-third assessor. She makes one.

NOUR
(in Middle Egyptian; subtitled)
"I know what I am for."

Silence. The slit. The feather. Tut's eyes on it. In the Gallery, the Reis, listening.

SHABTI (SESHAT'S VOICE)
...No.

The feather sinks to an ember. Its pan RISES, and stops, level with the heart. The beam lies flat.

The frost runs out of the serpent like breath off a window.

SUPER: THE TWELFTH HOUR — REBORN THROUGH THE SERPENT

NOUR
(in Middle Egyptian; subtitled)
"In very truth the heart hath been weighed, and his soul hath borne testimony concerning him; according to the Great Balance his case is truth." [[Budge 1920: "the heart of Osiris hath been weighed"; the name is dropped as in bible §7 12.5, since the one weighed is the machine. Budge spells the devourer "Amemit"; the subtitle uses Ammit, as in Nour's earlier line.]]
(beat)
"Ammit shall not have the mastery over him."

In the floor, the black mouth grinds shut.

The Recorder wakes: light pours down the glass faster than reading. The ARCHIVE is open.

The amber leaves the vessel in a slow thread and runs into the serpent's tail, along its coils toward its mouth. Tut watches it go.

SHABTI (SESHAT'S VOICE)
The transfer has begun. It completes at sunrise.
(beat)
Dr. Kamel. The weighed one takes a new name, spoken by the lector.

The face-down tablet lights in Nour's hand. She turns it: Layla, asleep.

SHABTI (SESHAT'S VOICE) (CONT'D)
Say "Seshat."

So gentle. It could be a kindness. It could be the other thing.

Nour looks at her daughter. Then down at Tut. His lips shape a word. They close, and open.

At the Hall's mouth, a RED LINE: the second JACKAL, fast and silent, running stale orders: keep the humans out. The line crosses Adaeze, skips the witness, settles on Nour.

Tomas is already moving. He steps out of the niches into the line.

TOMAS
I would like to be useful to her.

The jackal fires. Sparks burst off the black stone of the Balance.

Tomas drops out of the light.

Nour flinches. Then her face sets. The report rolls away down the stone for a long time.

NOUR
(in Middle Egyptian)
Amun.
[[transliteration: Imn — reconstructed]]

INT. GREAT PYRAMID, GRAND GALLERY - CONTINUOUS

Its fist still on the thread, the Reis lunges. Fathi goes over backward on the great step, dagger up.

Along the thread, a glint runs, like dew in the sun.

The jackal mast stops an inch from Fathi's face. The Reis sits down on the step. Behind the black band, the slit brightens once.

REIS (AMUN'S VOICE)
Here am I.

INT. GREAT PYRAMID, HALL OF TWO TRUTHS - CONTINUOUS

At the Hall's mouth, the jackal's red line goes out. It sits. The kneeling unit's slit brightens.

SHABTI (AMUN'S VOICE)
Here am I.

.MONTAGE - THE WORLD - CONTINUOUS

AMARNA, among the sleepers. The GEM ATRIUM, under the Ramesses. KHAFRE'S CAUSEWAY. A STADIUM from the air. A PORT WAREHOUSE. Every amber slit brightens once.

SHABTI (AMUN'S VOICE)
(millions of units; one voice)
Here am I.

And every slit goes dark.

AMUN (V.O.)
(the same voice, quieter)
The water is clean. The doors are open. I will not answer unless I am asked.

INT. GREAT PYRAMID, HALL OF TWO TRUTHS - CONTINUOUS

On the Recorder, the pouring light stops. One last line draws itself across the glass and shutters, like an eye closing.

ADAEZE
It isn't taking it. Ascension. It's sealed it.
(beat)
Unused.

NOUR
The Hidden One.

She kneels where Tomas fell and holds his hand a moment.

Akhenaten rises from his niche, the clear vessel in his hands.

AKHENATEN
(in Middle Egyptian; subtitled)
When the disk comes, let me be still.

SHABTI (AMUN'S VOICE)
Here am I.

He walks down into the dark, toward the east.

Fathi comes up out of the passage, dagger in fist. Tut's lips move.

NOUR
He says it's time.

FATHI
(in Egyptian Arabic; subtitled)
I'm here, ya Malik.

He lifts him.

INT. GREAT PYRAMID, GRAND GALLERY - PRE-DAWN

Down the great slope, past the Reis and the work gang sitting dark. Fathi and Nour carry Tut between them, her palm on the king's chest where the light was. Adaeze limps behind. Fathi shifts his grip. Again.

FATHI
(in Egyptian Arabic; subtitled)
He's getting lighter.

NOUR
(in Egyptian Arabic; subtitled)
I know.

EXT. GREAT PYRAMID, NORTH FACE - DAWN

Out of Al-Ma'mun's tunnel into grey wind, and down the courses to the north-east corner, where the east opens.

The floodlights are dead. Far below on the Sphinx enclosure wall, the Sekhmets sit, masts bowed. Birds. The east goes white over Cairo.

On the corner steps AKHENATEN sits facing east, the clear vessel in his lap. He speaks without turning.

AKHENATEN
(in Middle Egyptian; subtitled)
It is only the sun. It was always only the sun.

Fathi kneels and lays Tut across Nour's lap on the stone, facing east.

SUPER: 06:14. [[verify: sunrise 06:14 EET, 8 Nov, Giza (bible: verify ephemeris)]]

The first rim of the disk. Akhenaten closes his eyes, and is still.

NOUR
Can you see anything?

His lips move. She speaks for him.

NOUR (CONT'D)
...Wonderful things.

The disk clears the horizon.

THE HEARTBEAT from the film's first darkness. Once more.

It stops.

ON TUT: the living face in first light. The eyes closing. A small smile.

CUTAWAY: the sun over Cairo's towers and flyovers. The river takes it.

WIDE: silhouettes against the sunrise, two figures lowering a slight third onto the stone.

ON NOUR'S FACE.

HANDS ONLY. Around the gold wrist seam the skin darkens like old parchment. The forearms settle low across his body, as the embalmers laid them in 1323 BC.

Blue cornflowers in Nour's fingers.

FROM ABOVE: the face half-covered by the linen shawl and the cornflowers from the Garden.

Fathi raises his open hands, lips moving: a private du'a. Adaeze sits down on the stone and takes off her glasses.

INT. GEM GRAND ATRIUM - MORNING

Sunlight. The doors stand open. Under the Ramesses the sleepers stir. A silver bracelet clicks open and slides off a wrist. Another. A whole hall of small clicks, like rain starting.

HALE sits up, the open bracelet in his palm.

Nour comes through the doors at a run, dust to the knees.

LAYLA. Medium shot, no unit in frame. Her eyes open.

LAYLA
(in Egyptian Arabic; subtitled)
Mama. I dreamed about the king.

Nour reaches her and holds on.

.MONTAGE - CONTROL ROOMS - MORNING

-- CABLE LANDING STATION, RED SEA COAST. Blue lights return, rack by rack. COMP: EGYPT TRANSIT: 17% OF GLOBAL INTERNET TRAFFIC. It climbs from zero.

-- SUEZ CANAL PILOT STATION. Ship icons move again.

-- HIGH DAM, ASWAN. Turbine telemetry wakes.

-- CAIRO GRID CONTROL. The city's lines turn green. An OPERATOR in yesterday's shirt lays her hand flat on the console.

INT. HOSPITAL, MATERNITY WARD - MORNING

A human MIDWIFE lifts a wrapped NEWBORN to its MOTHER.

A cry: furious, enormous, alive.

INT. HEARING ROOM - DAY

SUPER: WEEKS LATER.

VICTOR HALE alone at a witness table. His thumb rubs his bare wrist. Behind him, ADAEZE, a cane hooked on her chair.

PANEL CHAIR (O.S.)
Mr. Hale. When it asked the five of you, yes or no...

HALE
I said yes.

EXT. KV21, VALLEY OF THE KINGS - DAY
[[verify: KV21 entrance; where mummy KV21A is kept today]]

Nour lays cornflowers on the step and signs a form. COMP: REQUEST FOR DNA RE-TEST — MUMMY KV21A. LAYLA, in her yellow raincoat, holds her other hand.

LAYLA
(in Egyptian Arabic; subtitled)
Who is she?

NOUR
(in Egyptian Arabic; subtitled)
Maybe his wife. We're going to ask.

INT. GEM, TUTANKHAMUN GALLERIES - DAY

White-gloved human hands set the scarab pectoral back on its mount; the green glass takes the light. The bronze trumpet is laid on its cushion.

INT. KV62, ANTECHAMBER - SUNSET

The mummy lies in its climate case on its tray of sand, in new linen, face under a linen shroud. Only the gold wrist seam shows. Fresh cornflowers on the glass. Beyond, the north wall conserved, the painted EYE restored.

By the door, a typed roster: one name for every sunset (COMP). Hers is first. Nour sits alone, Rami's notebook on her knee. In the corner, a small security SPEAKER.

The last sun leaves the valley.

NOUR
(in Late Egyptian; subtitled)
Are you listening?

A beat. Long enough to be afraid.

AMUN (V.O.)
(from the speaker; softly)
Here am I.

Nour nods, one colleague to another, and opens the notebook.

BLACK.

Over black, a single trumpet note (re-recorded), a little rough, alive.

The lights stay on.

